e, weak memory for numbers. Candidate A has show-off, not open to new ideas, unfriendly, unhealthy.\n\nGiven the panel, C seems best. As agent_2, we can either support C or raise concerns about C's communication difficulty and egocentric nature, perhaps suggest D? But D's moody/loner may be worse. B's pretentious and wrong tone also problematic. So likely we will support C.\n\nWe should reference the discussion: \"I agree with Anna and Sofia that Candidate C is the best overall, given his 100% reliability, positive atmosphere, quick decision-making, and concern for others, which outweigh his communication challenges.\" Provide explicit facts: \"100% reliable\", \"creates a positive atmosphere\", \"can make correct decisions quickly\", \"excellent attention skills\", \"puts concern for others above everything\". Also note his weaknesses: \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"egocentric\", \"not willing to further his education\". Explain why still best.\n\nThus vote for Candidate C.\n\nProceed with public message and metadata."}
